    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Counterparty EXPOSURE PROFILE over time via the each_step mode of the conditional nested-submodel statistic `nested_stat`. The outer model simulates a factor forward; at EACH timestep the inner submodel reprices a rolling position CONDITIONED on that step's factor level. The each_step nested element's time_history mean is the Expected-Exposure profile EE(t) and its p95 is the Potential-Future-Exposure PFE(t) \u2014 read straight from the per-step summary. Validated: EE(t)/PFE(t) reproduce the closed-form Black-Scholes profile at every step, and the terminal exposure tracks BS(S_H) per path. This is the per-(path,step) nested simulation the American tight dual and exposure/CVA analytics need. See NESTED_STAT_SCOPE.md."
  },
